text: |-
  R
  @ruthmayforth5933 • 38 min ago (edited)
  I am a surgeon. Based on the medical examiner's
  report, the trajectory & from the roof is NOT
  POSSIBLE.Charlie was hit in the low neck. The medical
  examiner's report said much of his cervical spine was
  traumatically gone, and the L side of C2-C7 was
  obliterated. To have affected up to C2, it would have
  had to be an upward trajectory from the point of entry
  on the neck. I heard a podcaster (Project Constitution)
  say that Charlie was also wearing a Rode transmitter at
  his L waist, if this had a shaped charge, the trajectory
  would make sense for entering the low neck and hitting
  his cervical spine.
  321
